articles.content_en:
When the People's Court adjudicates a case involving major disagreements among shareholders of a limited liability company, it shall emphasize mediation. Where the parties agree through consultation to resolve the disagreements by the following methods, and such methods do not violate the mandatory provisions of laws and administrative regulations, the People's Court shall support them:
(1) the company repurchases part of the shareholders' shares;
(2) other shareholders acquire part of the shareholders' shares;
(3) a third party acquires part of the shareholders' shares;
(4) the company reduces its capital;
(5) the company splits;
(6) other methods that can resolve the disagreements, restore the normal operation of the company, and avoid the dissolution of the company.
